.e2e-server.log.err
.e2e-audit/

# A local `dotnet run` with no CEDAR_DATA_DIR set puts its data dir inside the project — the SQLite
# file, uploaded media, and the DataProtection key ring that signs cookies and encrypts publish
# credentials. None of it belongs in the repo; production's lives on the Pi under CEDAR_DATA_DIR.
CedarClerk.Server/Data/dataprotection-keys/
CedarClerk.Server/Data/cedar.db
CedarClerk.Server/Data/cedar.db-shm
CedarClerk.Server/Data/cedar.db-wal
CedarClerk.Server/Data/media/
CedarClerk.Server/Data/import-tmp/

# === Desktop shell (T-121) ===
# The published server copied in beside the Electron shell by Scripts/build.ps1 — a build output,
# ~70MB of self-contained runtime, regenerated on every build.
CedarClerk.Desktop/server/

# === Marty's dynamic prompt inbox (18.08.2026) ===
